<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<%- include('_nav') %>
<main class="wrap adm-main adm-narrow">
  <h1 class="h2">How to run the website</h1>
  <% if (typeof flash !== 'undefined' && flash) { %><p class="notice notice-ok" role="status"><%= flash %></p><% } %>
  <div class="form adm-form prose">
    <h2 class="h3">Post a new job from your phone</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <strong><%= origin %>/admin</strong> on your phone and sign in.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Post a new job</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tap the photo box and pick the photos from your camera roll. Pick as many as you want.</li>
      <li>Type what the job was (“Kitchen remodel”), the town, and the year. Add a sentence or two about it if you like.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Post to the site</strong>. Wait for the photos to upload. It’s live.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Afterward you land on the job’s edit page, where you can drag photos into a better order, pick the cover photo, add captions, or add more photos.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Change the words on the site</h2>
    <p>While you’re signed in, every page of the site shows a blue bar at the top. Tap <strong>Edit this page’s text</strong>, click on any headline or paragraph, type, then tap <strong>Save changes</strong>. Visitors see the new text right away.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Estimate requests</h2>
    <p>When someone fills out the form on the Contact page, you get an email and it also shows up under <a href="/admin/leads">Estimate requests</a>. Reply to the email to answer them. Tap <strong>Mark done</strong> once you’ve handled it.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Rules we follow</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Never put a homeowner’s name or street address on the site. Town only. Businesses (churches, restaurants) can be named.</li>
      <li>Only our own photos.</li>
      <li>“Fully insured” is fine to say. Don’t make licensing claims.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h3">Phone numbers, emails, and who can sign in</h2>
    <p>All of that is under <a href="/admin/settings">Settings</a>. To let someone else sign in, make an invite link there and send it to them; they pick their own password.</p>
  </div>
</main>
</body></html>
